    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe new `contactPreference` method is placed correctly \u2014 it follows the established idiom in this mapper exactly (a `default` derivation method wired via an `@Mapping(expression = ...)`, alongside `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `bulkSignupWarning`), is well-scoped to one responsibility, and is documented consistently. The OpenAPI addition mirrors the surrounding `readOnly` derived fields. The one structural issue:\n\n- **Duplicated \"email is present\" predicate.** `contactPreference` (line 37) and `membershipLevel` (line 58) now both express the same business predicate verbatim: `owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank()`. This is the same concept (\"an email is present\") appearing in two derivations. Extract a small private/`default` helper, e.g. `hasEmail(Owner owner)`, and call it from both. That removes the duplication and keeps the two derivations in sync if the notion of \"present\" ever changes (e.g. trimming/whitespace rules).\n\nWith that single extraction the structure is clean.",
